BUNDLED RECORDINGS (Salah/Resources/Audio/)

The app plays these recordings for adhan alerts and the optional du'a after the adhan.
All seven came into this code base with the app it was rebuilt from, Guidance for Mac
by Batoul Apps. They are byte-identical to the files Batoul Apps' GuidanceMac repository
added on 24 October 2019 (commit 4de9e46). That repository's first commit, the same day
(a21eb77), added an MIT license, "Copyright (c) 2019 Batoul Apps". In November 2019 the
license and the recordings moved together into an oldVersion/ folder (e9633ea), and the
license file stayed there until the June 2026 rebuild this app comes from removed it
(2e7a290). Nothing in the repository names the recordings' original sources or the
terms under which Batoul Apps obtained them, and a license from Batoul Apps covers only
what Batoul Apps owned.

  File                 Shown in the app as   Source                          License
  Adhan-Alafasy.m4a    Mishary Alafasy       Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unconfirmed
  Adhan-Aqsa.mp3       Al-Aqsa               Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unconfirmed
  Adhan-Fajr.mp3       Fajr Adhan            Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unconfirmed
  Adhan-Istanbul.mp3   Istanbul              Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unconfirmed
  Adhan-Makkah.mp3     Makkah                Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unconfirmed
  Adhan-Yusuf.mp3      Yusuf Islam           Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unconfirmed
  Dua.m4a              (du'a after adhan)    Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unconfirmed

Adhan-Alafasy.m4a is a third-party recording, presented in the app as the adhan of
Mishary Rashid Alafasy; Adhan-Yusuf.mp3 is presented as Yusuf Islam's adhan.

Open question: the right to redistribute these recordings, Adhan-Alafasy.m4a in
particular, has not been confirmed. Confirm it with the rights holders, or replace the
recordings with ones whose terms are clear, before any App Store or other binary
release. The MIT License of this repository does not cover them.


LINKED CODE

SalahKit 0.4.0 (https://github.com/salah-kit/SalahKit) and SalahTimes 0.1.0
(https://github.com/salah-kit/SalahTimes), fetched by Swift Package Manager and linked
into the app and its widget extension: prayer-time calculation, the schedule, widget
timelines, alerts and UI building blocks. They are the salah-kit ecosystem's own
packages, by The Salah Kit Authors, under the same MIT License as this repository.
Salah links no third-party code. Until version 1.0.0, Salah calculated with adhan-swift
(https://github.com/batoulapps/adhan-swift, MIT, Copyright (c) 2016 Batoul Apps); it no
longer links it.
